From ee1f31fa1c53e708b04f5c6d5955b416629b7524 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:16:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Behaviours integrated on the device

A behaviour generated by the generic-parallel interface is integrated on
the copies of the arrays of its material on the device, if a device is
enabled in MFEM and if its computations can access them (a behaviour of
the cuda backend on a GPU, or any behaviour on the debug device of MFEM,
whose copies on the device are in the memory of the host): MGIS
integrates it on a view of these copies (make_unchecked_view, whose
views of the arrays are relocated on the copies made valid by MFEM), the
material properties, the external state variables and the mass density
being copied to the device at each call. The rotations of the
orthotropic behaviours are made on the device, as the computations of
the gradients and of the thermodynamic forces in the global frame when
the behaviour can't access the memory of the host.

The arrays of the materials are no longer synchronized on the host
before the integration when all the behaviours are integrated on the
device from gradients computed by kernels. After an integration on the
device, the arrays of the material are synchronized on the host for
reading if the inner forces or the stiffness matrices are computed by
the element loops of MFEM.

Tests: the behaviours of the openmp and stlpar backends are now tested
on the debug device of MFEM (copies on the device in the memory of the
host, accesses to invalid copies detected), and the behaviours of the
cuda backend on the GPU, sequentially and on two processes, with and
without kernels.
